WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:11.091
This page is your course map. Every week is a station on one journey, and because this section is fully self-paced, this page is also where you steer.

2
00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:22.124
Find the current week. The suggested-pace card names the week the calendar sits in. Click it, or click any station below, to open that week's page. The pace is a suggestion; the only fixed points are the two due dates.

3
00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:33.183
Read the station badge before you click. Each station shows its dates, how many readings it carries, and whether you have started it. The final project weeks carry no new material.

4
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:44.202
Track your driven weeks. The progress panel counts a week as driven once you check off its four steps on the week page. The two assessment windows under it show what is open and when it is due.

5
00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:55.204
Read the five moves. The orientation panel explains how to run a self-paced course well: you set the pace, the weekly experience carries the teaching, and you check your own understanding.

6
00:00:55.204 --> 00:01:06.216
Use the Study Compass. The compass box suggests what to do next based on what you have already done on this device. It is a suggestion, never a requirement. Adding your first name is optional.

7
00:01:06.216 --> 00:01:17.221
Pick your program lens if you want one. The Viewing as chip personalizes examples to your field of study. The course content stays the same for everyone; only the framing changes. You can turn it off any time.

8
00:01:17.221 --> 00:01:21.963
Nothing on this page is graded or reported to your professor.

9
00:01:21.963 --> 00:01:27.391
Where next: Open the current week's station and start its four-step path.
